<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bir Chandra Manikya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1837–1896</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bir Chandra Manikya was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripura">Tripura</a> from 1862 to 1896. He rebuilt <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agartala">Agartala</a> as a modern capital and introduced administrative reforms on the British Indian model. A poet, musician and early photographer, he was one of the first patrons of the young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rabindranath-tagore">Rabindranath Tagore</a>, beginning a long friendship between the Tripura court and the Tagore family.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bir-chandra-manikya.jpg" alt="Bir Chandra Manikya" width="220" height="360" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Court painter of Tripura · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maharaja_Bir_Chandra_Manikya.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
